01:53:18.507 --> 01:54:13.387
<v SPEAKER_14>Furthermore, he went into Ukraine, the Russian army went into Ukraine with at the very most 190,000 troops. There is absolutely no way he could have conquered all of Ukraine with 190,000 troops. When the Germans went into Poland on September 1st 1939, and you want to remember the Germans were only going to capture the western half of Poland, because the Soviet Union was going to capture the eastern half of Poland. So the Germans went into Poland September 1st 1939 to conquer it and incorporate it into a greater Germany with 1.5 million troops. Does anyone seriously believe that Putin with 190,000 troops at the very most was going to be able to conquer all of Ukraine, which is much bigger than Poland and certainly much bigger than the western half?

